<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial standards"
  description="How Belvoir Finance sources, reviews and corrects its stories, how it uses AI and what it discloses."
>
  <h1>Editorial standards</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <strong>Placeholder wording, awaiting editorial sign-off.</strong>
    </p>
    <h2>Sourcing</h2>
    <p>
      Stories are built from primary material wherever possible, and each story lists its sources with the date they
      were accessed. External feeds are research inputs and are never republished.
    </p>
    <h2>Review</h2>
    <p>
      Every factual finance story is checked by a named reviewer who is not its author before it is published. Each
      story shows when it was first published and last reviewed.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      When we find a mistake we correct the story and say what changed. There is no way to contact us yet; how to report
      a correction will be published here once it exists.
    </p>
    <h2>AI use</h2>
    <p>Nothing is published automatically. Any AI assistance is reviewed by a person before publication.</p>
    <h2>Disclosures</h2>
    <p>
      Belvoir Finance is the publisher of this site. Where a story touches a commercial interest, the story says so in a
      visible disclosure near the top of the page.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
